emblazonry.definition:
n. The act or art of an emblazoner; heraldic or ornamental
   decoration, as pictures or figures on shields, standards, etc.;
   emblazonment.

embolismical.definition:
a. Pertaining to embolism or intercalation;
   intercalated; as, an embolismic year, i. e., the year in which there is
   intercalation.
